---
import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro";
import { meta } from "../i18n/meta";
import { SITE_URL as siteUrl } from "../lib/site";
import { breadcrumbLd } from "../lib/breadcrumbs";
import { ogImageFor } from "../lib/og";

const m = meta.en.terms;

const pageLd = {
  "@context": "https://schema.org",
  "@type": "WebPage",
  name: m.title,
  description: m.description,
  inLanguage: "en",
  url: new URL("/terms-and-conditions", siteUrl).toString(),
  isPartOf: { "@id": `${siteUrl}/#website` },
};
---

<Layout
  title={m.title}
  description={m.description}
  ogImage={ogImageFor("/terms-and-conditions")}
  jsonLd={[
    breadcrumbLd("en", [
      { name: "Home", path: "/" },
      { name: "Terms & Conditions", path: "/terms-and-conditions" },
    ]),
    pageLd,
  ]}
>
  <main class="min-h-screen bg-canvas text-white">
    <section class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-4 py-16 sm:px-6 sm:py-24">
      <p
        class="font-mono text-[11px] font-semibold tracking-[1.8px] text-mint uppercase"
      >
        Legal
      </p>
      <h1
        class="mt-4 font-display text-5xl leading-[0.9] tracking-[1.07px] sm:text-6xl"
      >
        Terms &amp; Conditions
      </h1>
      <p class="mt-4 text-sm text-secondary">Last updated: 2026</p>

      <div
        class="mt-6 max-w-3xl space-y-4 text-sm leading-relaxed text-secondary"
      >
        <p>
          These terms govern your use of My World Cup XI, a free browser
          football game and World Cup draft simulator. They cover the game, the
          teams index, the how-to-play guide and every other page of the site.
          By using the site you agree to these terms. If you do not agree, do
          not use it. We wrote them in plain language.
        </p>
        <p>
          My World Cup XI is a free, non-commercial game made for fun. There are
          no accounts, purchases or real-money bets. If something is unclear,
          ask us on the contact page.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="mt-10 space-y-8 text-sm leading-relaxed text-secondary">
        <section>
          <h2 class="font-display text-xl tracking-[0.5px] text-white">
            1. Acceptance of terms
          </h2>
          <p class="mt-3">
            By using My World Cup XI (the "Site"), you agree to these Terms
            &amp; Conditions. If you do not agree, do not use the Site. Opening
            the game is enough to accept them. There is no account to create and
            no box to tick.
          </p>
          <p class="mt-3">
            These terms cover the whole site: the game, the draft, the teams
            index and the how-to-play guide. They work together with our Privacy
            Policy, which explains what little data the site uses. If a court
            finds one part invalid, the rest still applies. We may update these
            terms. The version on this page, with its "Last updated" date, is
            the one in force.
          </p>
          <p class="mt-3">
            Because the game is free, agreeing costs you nothing. It only asks
            you to use the site as described below. If you use the site for a
            school, club or community group, you confirm that you can accept
            these terms for that group. If you disagree with a change, stop
            playing and clear your storage. There is no account to close.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2 class="font-display text-xl tracking-[0.5px] text-white">
            2. Use of the service
          </h2>
          <p class="mt-3">
            The Site is a free, browser-based football simulator and World Cup
            simulator. It is for personal, non-commercial use. You may not use
            it to break any law or anyone's rights. You may not sell access to
            it, resell it, or include it in another product without permission.
          </p>
          <p class="mt-3">
            Do not use the site to harass others, scrape or overload our
            servers, or damage the app on other devices. Normal use is simple:
            open it, draft a squad, simulate a cup, share a screenshot of your
            result. Do not take apart the match engine to cheat. The squads and
            ratings are editorial, not official records.
          </p>
          <p class="mt-3">
            The teams index, the how-to-play guide and the draft tool are part
            of the same site, and the same personal-use rule applies to all of
            them. If you run a class, fan group or match-day event and want
            several people to use the game, that is welcome. Keep it
            non-commercial and lawful. If you are unsure whether a use fits, ask
            us before you build on it.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2 class="font-display text-xl tracking-[0.5px] text-white">
            3. No real-money transactions
          </h2>
          <p class="mt-3">
            The game simulates matches, drafts and tournaments. There is no real
            money, no prizes and no gambling. Results have no cash value. The
            site is a made-up World Cup game, not a betting product. We built it
            that way on purpose.
          </p>
          <p class="mt-3">
            The draft lets you build a dream XI from old squads, and the match
            engine decides a result. That result is for fun. We do not take
            deposits, run pools or sell paid entries. The words "fantasy" and
            "simulator" are deliberate: this is a free browser game with no
            download. The only stake is bragging rights with friends. If you
            want daily fantasy sports or any real-money contest, use a licensed
            operator in your area instead.
          </p>
          <p class="mt-3">
            Because the game is non-commercial, it suits classes and families.
            We may add shared, no-money challenges later, such as comparing cups
            with friends. They will never involve money, and we will explain any
            such feature before you use it.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2 class="font-display text-xl tracking-[0.5px] text-white">
            4. Intellectual property
          </h2>
          <p class="mt-3">
            All content on the Site is ours or licensed to us. That includes the
            game engine, design, text and code. It is protected by law. You may
            not copy, reuse or share it without permission. The game, the draft,
            the teams index and the how-to-play guide are original works. The
            match engine is our own code.
          </p>
          <p class="mt-3">
            You may share your own results, such as a screenshot of a trophy or
            a story about a Brazil 1970 run. You may not take the code, the
            player-rating data or the visual design and present them as your
            own.
          </p>
          <p class="mt-3">
            Player, team and tournament names belong to their owners. We use
            them for description only. "FIFA", "EA Sports" and "Football
            Manager" are trademarks of their owners, and this site is not
            affiliated with any of them. The old squads are content you put on
            the pitch and simulate. They are not official records, and the
            ratings are game estimates tuned for balance.
          </p>
          <p class="mt-3">
            If you write about the game, run a lesson or host a community event,
            you may describe and link to the site. You may not redistribute the
            app or imply a partnership.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2 class="font-display text-xl tracking-[0.5px] text-white">
            5. No warranty
          </h2>
          <p class="mt-3">
            The Site is provided "as is" and "as available". We make no
            warranties, stated or implied. We do not promise that the site will
            never stop, never error, or be free of harm. We do not promise that
            the simulation will match real events. It is fun software, not a
            forecast. A draft beating a higher-rated AI side is a result of the
            match engine, not a prediction of a real tournament.
          </p>
          <p class="mt-3">
            We try to keep the game stable and the penalty shootouts fair, but
            we cannot promise that the app will never glitch across every
            browser and device. We also cannot promise that the editorial player
            ratings match an official source. They are tuned for balance inside
            the game, not copied from records.
          </p>
          <p class="mt-3">
            Where the law allows, we disclaim implied warranties. Use the game
            for fun, not for reliance. If a bug affects a saved cup, clearing
            storage and starting a new draft usually fixes it. Your data is
            local, so the reset is clean. Nothing here cuts consumer rights you
            have under local law. Those always apply.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2 class="font-display text-xl tracking-[0.5px] text-white">
            6. Limitation of liability
          </h2>
          <p class="mt-3">
            To the fullest extent the law allows, we are not liable for damages
            from your use of the Site. The game is free, has no account, and
            stores your drafts on your device. The most you can usually lose
            from a fault is the time spent on one cup.
          </p>
          <p class="mt-3">
            We are not liable for indirect or follow-on losses, such as a
            simulated result affecting an office pool or the game being
            unavailable when you want to play. We are also not responsible for
            how you interpret the editorial squads or player ratings. They are
            game estimates, not official stats. Nothing here limits liability
            that the law says we cannot exclude, and nothing here affects rights
            the law gives you.
          </p>
          <p class="mt-3">
            Because the game is free and local, the real risk to you is small.
            If a problem occurs, contact us and we will look into it. The game
            improves most from real reports.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2 class="font-display text-xl tracking-[0.5px] text-white">
            7. Changes
          </h2>
          <p class="mt-3">
            We may change these terms at any time. If you keep using the Site
            after a change, you accept the new terms. When we update, we refresh
            the "Last updated" date at the top so you can see which version is
            in force. If a change is significant, such as adding a feature that
            changes the personal, non-commercial nature of the site, we will say
            so clearly and ask first where the law requires it. Small changes,
            such as a wording fix or a new formation, may happen without notice.
          </p>
          <p class="mt-3">
            Check back now and then, especially if you use the teams index or
            the how-to-play guide as a reference. The main points will not
            change: the game stays free, stays non-commercial, and keeps your
            drafts on your device. If you disagree with an update, stop playing
            and clear your storage. There is no account to close and no download
            to uninstall.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2 class="font-display text-xl tracking-[0.5px] text-white">
            8. Contact
          </h2>
          <p class="mt-3">
            Questions about these terms or how the site should be used? We can
            explain any clause in plain words. The contact page is the fastest
            way to reach us. Ask about a wording question or suggest a feature.
          </p>
          <p class="mt-3">
            The game has no account, so there is nothing to cancel if you
            disagree with a change. Stop playing and clear your storage.
          </p>
          <p class="mt-3">
            We welcome notes from parents, teachers and group leaders who use
            the game in class or on match day. We read every message. These
            terms are not a wall between us and the players. They are the shared
            deal that keeps the game fair and free.
          </p>
          <p class="mt-3">
            If something here is unclear, tell us in everyday language and we
            will answer the same way. <a
              class="text-mint underline"
              href="/contact/">Contact us</a
            > and help keep the game open and fun.
          </p>
        </section>
      </div>
    </section>
  </main></Layout
>
